body: "# Sprint 8.0 + 8.1.1 Foundation — Premium-Elite Substrate\n\n## Outcome\nSprint 8.0 foundation + first canonical parser (CAPEX) SHIPPED with 18/18 tests PASS.\nCell-level provenance chain operational: every numeric data cell extracted from MEF\nworkbook becomes an `AnchoredValue` with full provenance (workbook + sheet + A1 address\n+ row_label + year + formula + neighbours + confidence).\n\n## Sprint 8.0 Deliverables\n\n| File | LOC | Tests | Purpose |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| address.rs (NEW) | ~140 | 8 | A1 notation: col_letter, cell_address, parse_address, sheet_qualified |\n| schema_trait.rs (NEW) | ~210 | 4 | SheetSchema trait + AnchoredValue + Neighbours + helpers |\n| parser_generic.rs (EXT) | +90 | (compile) | parse_sheet_full, iter_provenance, formula_cell_count |\n| mod.rs (EDIT) | +10 | — | re-exports for both new modules |\n| **8.0 TOTAL** | **~450** | **12** | Foundation ready |\n\n## Sprint 8.1.1 Deliverable\n\n| File | LOC | Tests | Pattern |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| parsers/capex.rs (REWRITE) | ~330 | 6 | CapexParser implements SheetSchema TIMELINE pattern |\n\n## Architectural pattern established\n\n`AnchoredValue` schema (the atomic unit of evidence):\n```rust\n{\n  workbook: String,           // \"RMS_Corredor Interestadual - MEF (20260223).xlsm\"\n  sheet: String,              // \"CAPEX\"\n  cell_address: String,       // \"C4\"\n  row: usize, col: usize,     // 3, 2\n  canonical_field: String,    // \"capex_total_year_2027\"\n  value: TypedCell::Number(760.32),\n  formula: Some(\"=SUM(B5:B11)\") OR None,\n  confidence: 0.95,\n  neighbours: { left: \"0\", right: ..., up: ..., down: ... }\n}\n```\n\nEvery numerical claim in Voto v2.0 will be traceable through this chain.\n\n## Sprint 8 remaining roadmap\n\n| Sub | Scope | Pattern | LOC est | Tests est |\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| **8.1.2-8.1.6** | OPEX, Receitas, Cronograma, Demanda-OD, RESUMO | timeline_extractor.rs shared helper, then thin parsers | ~600 | ~30 |\n| **8.2** | WACC, Painel Controle, Tarifas, Cronograma, Fluxo Caixa, Depreciação, CAPEX Capital/LCC/Frota, OPEX Ambiental, Balanço, Fretes | scatter_extractor.rs for FORMULA_HEAVY | ~800 | ~40 |\n| **8.3** | 11 long-tail parsers (Capa, Trecho, Frota, Gráficos, etc.) | mostly thin | ~700 | ~35 |\n| **8.4** | PyO3 expansion: extract_canonical, cell_at, audit_trail, get_formulas | new bindings | ~200 | ~10 |\n| **8.5** | Cross-corridor diff (workbook_diff, consolidate) | new top-level | ~300 | ~15 |\n| **8.6** | Python semantic_layer becomes thin wrapper (net -500 LOC) | refactor | -500 | — |\n| **8.7** | E2E validation + benchmark | tests + bench | ~200 | ~20 |\n| **TOTAL REMAINING** | — | — | **~2300 LOC** | **~150 tests** |\n\n## Validation passing\n\n- cargo check --features mef-rail = 2.18s\n- cargo test --features mef-rail --lib mef_rail = 18/18 PASS\n- All public symbols re-exported via mod.rs\n- panic!() detected in tests only (unwrap on test fixtures, not production paths)\n\n## Lessons captured\n\nL33: REGRA #11 → use `taco-forge perfect-edit --operation free-form --content-from staging.txt` to replace .rs files (canonical alternative to Write).\n\nL34: taco-forge requires ABSOLUTE paths when invoked outside workspace root (`cd .` confused path resolution).\n\nL35: calamine `Range::get_value((r, c))` is absolute coords (not relative to start). `Range::from_sparse(cells)` for test fixtures.\n"
